WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.939 --> 00:00:07.769
One of the best things on TV is Impractical
Jokers, a hidden camera show featuring four

00:00:07.769 --> 00:00:12.530
lifelong friends who challenge each other
to engage in embarrassing situations. Because

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:16.250
of the revealing nature of the show, there
are very few parts of the Jokers' private

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.230
lives that aren't on public display, but here
are a few things you may not have known about

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:23.600
America's funniest friends.
Comic Book Man

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.870
AMC's Comic Book Men almost featured another
member, but Brian "Q" Quinn was stuck in TruTV's

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:32.930
contractual grip and couldn't join his good
friends on Kevin Smith's nerdy version of

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:39.059
Pawn Stars. Q, a lifelong fan of comics, appears
regularly on a podcast called Tell 'Em Steve-Dave

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:41.789
with Comic Book Men's Walt Flanagan and Bryan
Johnson.

00:00:41.789 --> 00:00:43.420
Q's First Girlfriend

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:46.969
Astute viewers will note that Q has mentioned
that his first girlfriend spent some time

00:00:46.969 --> 00:00:49.869
in prison, and that she's the half-sister
of an A-list celebrity.:

00:00:49.869 --> 00:00:52.809
"I know who it is, and I know where she is!"

00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:55.000
"Hahahahaha prison!"

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.280
"She's in prison!"

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.860
"She's alive and breathing!"

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:01.020
Out of respect forthe delicate family situation, Q's never mentioned her

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.139
by name on the air. However, dedicated

00:01:03.139 --> 00:01:07.540
Redditors have used information from the show
and Q's podcast to limit the possibilities

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:13.000
to a very specific area at a very specific
time, and deduced that Q dated King of Queens

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.050
star Leah Remini's half-sister Elizabeth,
who was arrested in 2005 for felonious cocaine

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:21.360
trafficking. But you didn't hear it from us...

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.670
Brian's Swollen Brain

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:26.960
There were a few Jokers episodes where it
was very clear that Q was suffering from an

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:31.340
illness, and at least one challenge that Q
was allowed to skip because of health concerns.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:35.580
Viewers didn't know that Q's problems were
far worse than the flu, and after a battery

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:41.020
of invasive tests administered by four doctors,
a regimen of serious antibiotics, and a misdiagnosis

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:46.680
of Lyme disease, Q found out he was actually
suffering from serious encephalitis and meningitis.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:51.200
The difference between pre- and post-illness
Q was about 15 pounds, and Jokers filming

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.660
was put off for about 
a week.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:56.000
"uuhhhh, one last ride then it's night night forever."

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.060
"See you soon, ma!"

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.060
Full Cup

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:05.980
Between 2010 and 2014, Joker Sal Vulcano was
a part owner of Full Cup, a beloved music

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.259
venue and bar in his native Staten Island.
Unfortunately, the location ran into financial

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:16.480
trouble in 2014 and rebranded itself as Hashtag
Bar in early 2016. Sal mentioned the bar in

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:22.000
his 2013 Reddit AMA, but once the bar started
to crash and burn in 2014, he made a public

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.940
statement saying he hadn't been involved in
operations for more than a year. He ditched

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:29.980
the struggling business, taking his finance
degree with him, and completely embraced his

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.130
new life of TV torture.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.060
Sal's Tats

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.480
One of the most memorable punishments in Jokers
history involved three of the castmembers

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:41.980
getting tattoos determined by Joe Gatto, who
was the only winner of that week's challenge.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.730
While Q and Murr's tattoos were meaningful
to their lives in a sarcastic way, Sal's tattoo

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:51.760
was a huge picture of Jaden Smith on his thigh.
Viewers will also notice that Sal already

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:57.020
had quite a few tattoos at this point, including
tribal bands around his calves. His arm tattoo,

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:01.180
however, has a pretty deep meaning to him:
it's song lyrics dedicated to a friend that

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:06.490
he lost in 2011. Kinda makes that Jaden tattoo
look especially cruel.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:07.290
Slap Attack

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:11.340
Even though most of the pranks on Jokers are
designed to only embarrass the four stars,

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.280
there have been plenty of times when they've
almost come to blows with the unsuspecting

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.819
public—and twice when they did. Anyone who
watches the show knows that all four friends

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:24.040
are really polite, respectful guys, but Sal
was once slapped when he was forced to tell

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.630
a woman that her baby was ugly, and also choked
by a man that he'd cut in line as part of

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:32.770
a challenge. Apologies were quickly dispensed,
and neither segment aired.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:33.340
Crydiving

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:38.819
Murr's most notable punishment, and the inspiration
for his tattoo, was being forced to skydive

00:03:38.819 --> 00:03:40.839
despite a serious fear of heights:

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.240
"Geronimoooo!"

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:51.180
"Aaaahhh! Aaahhh! Aaaah!"

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:54.980
On air, we see Murr run and threaten to quit the show,

00:03:54.989 --> 00:03:59.069
but what we don't see is the hour he spent
locked in a bathroom, refusing to come out

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:03.510
while he sent farewell texts to his friends
and family, sure that he would not survive

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:07.849
the experience. Both Murr and Sal share a
fear of heights, which they'd face again during

00:04:07.849 --> 00:04:10.760
their later charitable tightrope walk.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.080
MurrTV

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.509
In their tour documentary, the Jokers credit
James Murray as being the unstoppable force

00:04:16.509 --> 00:04:21.190
behind getting Impractical Jokers on the air.
Despite being a reality TV star, Murr still

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:25.570
maintains his day job as the Senior VP of
Development at North South Productions, which

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.710
explains why he's the only Joker too busy
to have his own podcast, even though he could

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:34.320
host one in any of the 17 languages he claims
to be able to speak. That is, when he’s

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.880
not shot full of Novocain:

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:36.980
"Braised beef"

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:37.980
"Is brilliant"

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.120
"Is...Braised bre..."

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:42.720
"Braised breef is brr..."

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:44.620
"Hahaha!"

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.660
"Braised breef is brilliant"

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:49.660
"Hahaha!"

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.440
"I said it once I'll say it again!"

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.180
"I said it once I'll say it again!"

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.740
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:58.699
channel to watch more videos like the one
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let

00:04:58.699 --> 00:05:00.470
us know which Jokers moment is your favorite...

